{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #388: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Can one classify all solutions of\\[\\prod_{1\\leq i\\leq k_1}(m_1+i)=\\prod_{1\\leq j\\leq k_2}(m_2+j)\\]where $k_1,k_2>3$ and $m_1+k_1\\leq m_2$? Are there only finitely many solutions? Current best: More generally, if $k_1>2$ then for fixed $a$ and $b$\\[a\\prod_{1\\leq i\\leq k_1}(m_1+i)=b\\prod_{1\\leq j\\leq k_2}(m_2+j)\\]should have only a finite number of solutions. Prize: no. Tags: number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_ac96c2a0d6fc8692ba5cb98b0ed46b9adc8d4ca92f90c4cf071f7321bd9d3470","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:388","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_326e38173e8038ec","object_root":"sha256:146c987d85bbe7e9a51c9328819f50639272ddc32fe57017a59088cbe34c48c5","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:388"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}